## Summary

I fixed the server crash in `singleValueOrNull` with the `JSON` type by correcting two type mismatches in `src/AggregateFunctions/AggregateFunctionSingleValueOrNull.cpp`:

**1. `deserialize` (line 172) — the segfault fix**
```cpp
// before
data(place).read(buf, *serialization, result_type, arena);
// after
data(place).read(buf, *serialization, value_type, arena);
```
The `serialization` member is built from the non-nullable `value_type` (`type->getDefaultSerialization()`), but `read` was being handed `result_type`, which is `makeNullable(type)`. For `JSON`, feeding the serialization a mismatched (nullable-wrapped) type during deserialization is what caused the `singleValueOrNullMerge` segfault. Passing `value_type` makes the type consistent with the serialization used on the write path.

**2. `insertResultInto` (line 95) — nested-column type consistency**
```cpp
// before
data().insertResultInto(col.getNestedColumn(), result_type);
// after
data().insertResultInto(col.getNestedColumn(), removeNullable(result_type));
```
The result is inserted into `col.getNestedColumn()` — the non-nullable nested column of the `ColumnNullable` — so it must receive the non-nullable type via `removeNullable`, not the nullable `result_type`. `removeNullable` is already available through the included `DataTypeNullable.h`.

